 ## Existing installations and restore
 
+Inspect a personal installation without changing source files, host entries, directories,
+or restoration receipts. Specify the home to inspect; an explicit `--home` ignores inherited
+`CODEX_HOME`, and `--codex-home` can select a custom Codex directory:
+
+```bash
+python3 install.py status --target codex --skill documentation-skill --home /path/to/home
+python3 install.py status --target codex --all --home /path/to/home --codex-home /path/to/codex --json
+python3 install.py status --target copilot --all --home /path/to/home
+```
+
+Repeated `--skill` flags, deprecated selector aliases, and automatic dependencies match
+installation selection. The report covers only the selected canonical skill and role
+destinations; Copilot is skill-only. Each entry is `current`, `missing`, or `different`.
+Current skills must be symlinks with the installer's canonical absolute source-directory
+target; equivalent relative symlinks report `different`. Current Codex roles must be regular
+hardlinks sharing the current source inode. A copied role, role symlink, or stale hardlink
+after atomic source replacement is `different`, even when its bytes still match.
+
+Human output is the default. `--json` emits one object with `schema_version: 1` and `entries`
+sorted by `area` then `name`; each entry contains `area`, `name`, and `state`. A validation or
+filesystem error returns an empty `entries` array plus an `error` string and a diagnostic on
+stderr. Exit status is zero only when every expected entry is current, and nonzero for
+missing, different, or invalid inspection requests. Invalid CLI syntax uses normal argparse
+usage errors. Symlinked or non-directory destination ancestors are invalid layouts.
+
+This is a point-in-time linkage inspection, not a content audit, host-discovery check, or
+ownership decision. It does not inspect legacy or unselected entries, interpret receipts,
+distinguish outdated owned entries from user modifications, grant overwrite permission, or
+repair entries. In-place source edits remain current because their linkage remains intact;
+concurrent filesystem changes can invalidate a completed report.
+
